  "name": "Question 10",
  "problem": "Find the values of $x$ for which the function $f(x)=5-7x-4{x}^{2}$ is strictly decreasing.",
  "worked_solution": "The function is strictly decreasing where ${f}^{\u2032}(x)<0.$ Differentiating $f(x),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(x) & =-7-8x \\\\  & =-8(x+\\frac{7}{8}),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso we need to solve the inequality\n\n$$\n-8(x+\\frac{7}{8})<0.\n$$\n\nSolving this inequality, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-8(x+\\frac{7}{8}) & <0 \\\\ 0 & <8(x+\\frac{7}{8}) \\\\ 0 & <x+\\frac{7}{8} \\\\ -\\frac{7}{8} & <x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that $f(x)$ is strictly decreasing on the interval $x\\in (-\\frac{7}{8},\\infty ).$",
